REFINERY SAFETY STANDARD OPERATING PROCEDURE (SOP-REF-2026)
DOCUMENT CONTROL NUMBER: ABC-SOP-409
EFFECTIVE DATE: JANUARY 2026

SECTION 4: EMERGENCY SHUTDOWN AND ISOLATION PROCEDURES
Section 4.1 General Safety Policy
All high-pressure pumps operating in Refinery Unit 4B must be monitored continuously for vibration, pressure, and mechanical seal fluid leakage.

Section 4.2 Mandatory Pump Immediate Shutdown Criteria
An immediate emergency shutdown of high-pressure pumps (such as Pump P-102A) must be initiated by the Shift Engineer upon occurrence of ANY of the following triggering conditions:
1. Discharge Pressure exceeding 45.0 BAR (Maximum Allowable Operating Pressure limit).
2. Vibration Spectrum Analysis indicating bearing wear level exceeding 70.0% of replacement threshold.
3. Uncontrolled mechanical seal leakage rate exceeding 1.5 Liters per Hour.
4. Bearing housing temperature exceeding 85.0 degrees Celsius.

Section 4.3 Swapping Procedures
Upon initiating emergency shutdown of primary pump P-102A:
- Open bypass valve B-12 to equalize pressure across auxiliary line.
- Engage auxiliary pump P-102B within 24 hours to maintain refinery throughput.
- Issue formal approval note for maintenance expedition.
